TEST_START: local party core / local lobby enforces capacity, readiness and match roster
TEST_START: local party core / one short cup, one optional double final, no duplicate rewards
TEST_START: local party core / tied leaders play a separate remapped reaction round
TEST_START: local party core / repeated true draws terminate fairly
TEST_START: local party core / aborted and malformed results never advance the cup
TEST_START: local party core / short party races explicitly opt in without changing ordinary races
TEST_START: local party core / first-to-cups ends early and ranks by cups, not points
TEST_START: local party core / simultaneous cup target launches a deciding round
TEST_START: local party core / legacy tournament save restores as fixed-points mode
TEST_START: local party core / JSON round trip resumes the exact next game and rules
TEST_START: local party core / favorites are unique, local, and exclude bosses
TEST_START: local party core / battery saver is a reversible effective override
TEST_START: local party core / every named human earns their own stats; guests earn no host stats
TEST_START: local party core / eight recognizable archetypes with bounded perks and equal budgets
TEST_START: local party core / all game controls fit separate local regions in both orientations
TEST_START: local party core / four touch sources keep fingers and input frames independent
TEST_START: local party core / global touch events isolate four simultaneous movement and fire controls in both orientations
TEST_START: local party core / pooled shells reset variant state
TEST_START: local party core / tank ammo variants use the same match and bounded projectile pool
TEST_START: local party core / background pause releases every finger and settings preserve the match
TEST_START: local party core / wide local arenas frame every competitor outside touch and score strips
TEST_START: local party core / collector skill chooses less-contested visible loot without hidden buffs
TEST_START: local party core / base default methods do not count as a game's scoring implementation

